---
description: Require security checks and multi-level testing for Capacitor and live-update changes
alwaysApply: true
---

capacitor-security-and-testing:

- Never store secrets, auth tokens, or credentials in plain `Preferences`, `localStorage`, or logs.
- Require HTTPS-first networking and secure production defaults (`cleartext: false`, restricted allow-lists).
- Run security scans for release candidates and treat high/critical findings as blockers.
- Ensure WebView debugging and verbose native logging are disabled for release builds.
- Add or update tests at the right layer: unit tests for logic, integration tests for plugin bridges, E2E/smoke tests for flows.
- For live updates, validate startup health and rollback behavior on at least one iOS and one Android build.
